        "text": "The simplest option is Time Machine, which keeps hourly and daily copies on an external drive.\nA bootable clone copies the whole disk, so you can start from it if your Mac fails.\niCloud keeps your Documents, Desktop, Photos and more in sync, but it is not a full backup.\nThird-party cloud services back up everything on the Mac to an online server for a monthly fee.\n",
